# 🎯 DBMS PYQ PRACTICE

## Q1 ⭐

A relation has attributes:

$$
(A,B,C)
$$

Functional dependencies:

$$
A\rightarrow B
$$

$$
B\rightarrow C
$$

Which dependency is transitive?

### Answer

$$
A\rightarrow B\rightarrow C
$$

Therefore:

$$
\boxed{A\rightarrow C}
$$

This is a **transitive dependency**.

---

## Q2 ⭐

A schedule has a precedence graph containing a cycle.

Is it conflict serializable?

### Answer:

$$
\boxed{\text{No}}
$$

### Rule:

> **Cycle = Not conflict serializable**

---

## Q3 ⭐⭐

Which ACID property ensures that committed data survives a crash?

$$
\boxed{\text{Durability}}
$$

---

## Q4 ⭐⭐

Transaction T1 reads uncommitted data written by T2.

What problem is this?

$$
\boxed{\text{Dirty Read}}
$$

---

## Q5 ⭐⭐⭐

A relation is in 2NF but has:

$$
A\rightarrow B
$$

$$
B\rightarrow C
$$

where B is not a candidate key.

Which normal form is violated?

$$
\boxed{\text{3NF}}
$$

Because of **transitive dependency**.

