# 💻 CODING PRACTICE FOR TODAY

## Easy DSA Revision: Two Sum

### Problem

Given an array and a target, find two numbers whose sum equals the target.

### Optimal Python Solution

```python
def twoSum(nums, target):
    seen = {}

    for i, num in enumerate(nums):
        need = target - num

        if need in seen:
            return [seen[need], i]

        seen[num] = i
```

### Complexity

$$
\boxed{O(n)\text{ Time}}
$$

$$
\boxed{O(n)\text{ Space}}
$$

### 🧠 Pattern

```text
Array + Target Sum
        ↓
      HashMap
```

This pattern appears frequently in coding interviews.

